Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

eeemail forks and depends on components from the Delta Chat / chatmail project
and its ecosystem. Each retains its own license.

  chatmail/core (forked into core/)      MPL-2.0
    https://github.com/chatmail/core
    Delta Chat core library: Autocrypt, SecureJoin, PGP/MIME, IMAP/SMTP,
    ephemeral messages, MDN, multi-device sync, encrypted backup, WebRTC calls.

  chatmail/relay (adapted into server/)  MPL-2.0
    https://github.com/chatmail/relay
    Postfix/Dovecot/OpenDKIM/filtermail configuration and deployment tooling.

  deltachat-contact-tools                MPL-2.0
  format-flowed                          MPL-2.0

  rPGP (pgp)                             MIT OR Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/rpgp/rpgp
  async-imap                             MIT OR Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/chatmail/async-imap
  async-smtp                             MIT OR Apache-2.0

Protocol specifications implemented:

  SecureJoin      https://securejoin.delta.chat/          (CC)
  Autocrypt L1.1  https://docs.autocrypt.org/level1.html  (CC0)
  RFC 8098 (MDN), RFC 9788 (header protection), RFC 3156 (PGP/MIME),
  RFC 3676 (format=flowed), RFC 9580 (OpenPGP)

The full dependency tree and its licenses can be regenerated with
`cargo about generate` or `cargo deny list` once the workspace exists.
